    "updated_at": "2016-05-13T17:06:08Z",
    "body": "What we really need, as alluded to in that bug, is a \"design doc\" for what the desired data is. E.g., it should include samples of the output, including hard cases (like those denoted by asterisks in the indices, or differentiating \"globals\" vs. concrete attribute names like \"href\").\n\nThis is a good idea though. I just wish it was concrete.\n",
